WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.464
A class has twelve girls and eighteen boys. A ratio compares two amounts. Girls to boys is twelve to eighteen. We write twelve colon eighteen. The order matters. It follows the words of the question, so girls come first.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:38.958
A ratio should always be simplified. Divide both numbers by the highest common factor. That is the biggest number that divides exactly into both. For twelve and eighteen it is six. So twelve to eighteen simplifies to two to three.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:50.387
Be careful with the words all and the rest. A ratio of girls to all children uses the total as the second number. A ratio of girls to the rest uses the total minus the girls.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:01:01.098
This question type says: calculate the ratio of one group to another. You find both amounts, write them in order, and simplify.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:20.570
Step one: work out both amounts, in the order asked. Step two: write them as a colon b. This shows your method. Step three: divide both by the highest common factor, so the ratio is in its simplest form.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:30.902
The trap is the word all. Ratio to all participants uses the total. Many students use the rest instead, and lose the mark.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:49.543
Here is a real exam question. Thomas tests whether a man's clothes affect obedience. We calculate the ratio of participants who disobeyed, to all participants taking part. It is worth two marks.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:59.598
Here are the results. The question asks for those who disobeyed. That is the disobeyed column: eight in Condition A and nineteen in Condition B.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:09.390
Step one. Both amounts. Disobeyed is eight plus nineteen, which is twenty seven. All participants is the whole group, sixty.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:18.141
Step two. Write the ratio in the order asked: disobeyed first, then all. Twenty seven colon sixty.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:36.692
Step three. Simplify. The highest common factor of twenty seven and sixty is three. Twenty seven divided by three is nine. Sixty divided by three is twenty. Nine and twenty share no other factor, so nine colon twenty is fully simplified.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:49.741
A tempting wrong route is disobeyed to obeyed, twenty seven to thirty three. That compares the group to the rest. But the question says to all participants, so the second number must be sixty.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:03:05.740
Now the exam-ready answer. Disobeyed equals eight plus nineteen, which is twenty seven. All equals sixty. Twenty seven colon sixty simplifies to nine colon twenty. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:24.464
A common mistake is to simplify only part of the way. Twelve to thirty can be divided by three to give four to ten. But four and ten still share the factor two. Divide by the highest common factor, six, to reach two to five.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:42.306
Now you try. Andrew had twenty participants in his memory experiment. A quarter of them were male. Calculate the ratio of males to females. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:54.313
First find both amounts. A quarter of twenty is twenty divided by four, which is five males. The rest are females: twenty minus five is fifteen.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:04.331
Now write males to females: five colon fifteen. The highest common factor is five. So the ratio simplifies to one colon three.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:19.983
A common wrong answer is one to four. That is males to all, because a quarter is one in four. But the question asks for males to females. Females are the rest, fifteen, not twenty. So it loses the mark.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:28.886
So find both amounts. Write a colon b in the order asked. Simplify by the highest common factor.
